  "summary": "The Ithaca Common Council voted to end the city's contract with Flock Safety, citing privacy concerns, data-sharing provisions, and conflicts with Ithaca's sanctuary city policies. The resolution's sponsor pointed to Flock data being used for immigration enforcement elsewhere as a key reason.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Ithaca is the latest city to end its relationship with Flock Safety over privacy and data-sharing concerns.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "I don't know that I could live with myself if I allowed something to exist in our community that directly or indirectly led to someone's civil liberties being violated",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
